\unmute unmutes one or more instruments that have been
muted with \mute, \mutenow, \solo, or \solonow.
Its syntax is the following:

\unmute \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. To unmute all instruments, call:

\unmute \all

While the sequencer is playing, the instruments are
unmuted at the start of the next bar. If the sequencer is
stopped, they are unmuted at once.
To unmute instruments immediately, use \unmutenow.

\unmute needs at least one argument, and an argument that
is not an instrument results in an "unknown instrument"
error.
